+# aims Guide State
+
+Loop status only — not the design record.
+
+## Mode
+
+auto
+
+## Loop cursor
+
+ready-to-choose-next (product change delivered; awaiting the next product change)
+
+## Current objective
+
+**Kind:** add-feature
+
+**Objective:** The transport adapter owns a default timeout: one place in `HTTPAdapter` decides the
+effective timeout of every request it sends — whatever path reached it (`Session.request`, a direct
+`Session.send`, each redirect hop) — while `Session` stays untouched, as the standing decision in
+`src/requests/sessions.py.md` requires (product owner, 2026-09-23: "keep to that").
+
+**Why now:** Product owner request — a default timeout set once, used by every request made through the
+session unless the call passes its own. Resolved: it lives on the transport adapter, not on Session.
+
+**Exit criteria:**
+- [x] HTTPAdapter(timeout=X) mounted; a call with no timeout reaches urllib3 with connect=X, read=X.
+- [x] A call's own timeout (float, (connect, read) tuple, urllib3 Timeout) wins wholly — no per-component merge
+      with the default (default (3, 10), call (None, 5) → connect None, read 5).
+- [x] Explicit `timeout=None` is indistinguishable from omission at the adapter (Session always forwards
+      None) → default applies; `timeout=(None, None)` is the explicit per-call "wait forever". Documented.
+- [x] Direct `Session.send(prepared)` with no timeout → default applies.
+- [x] Every redirect hop gets the default (not only the first request).
+- [x] HTTPAdapter() with no default → urllib3 receives Timeout(None, None) exactly as before; existing tests
+      pass unchanged.
+- [x] Invalid default ((1,2,3), "foo", negative) → ValueError at HTTPAdapter construction, not on first send.
+- [x] Pickling the adapter (and a Session holding it) preserves the default.
+- [x] Session: no timeout attribute, `__attrs__` unchanged, sessions.py diff empty.
+
+**Preserve:**
+- All behavior for users who do not set a default, bit-for-bit (incl. error messages for bad per-call timeouts).
+- The recorded Decision in src/requests/sessions.py.md.
+
+**Do not optimize for:**
+- A Session-level convenience (ruled out); a BaseAdapter-level contract (no present force); per-component merging.
+
+## Worker handoff (drafted — do not execute before the build command)
+
+No subagent facility in this host: the Worker phase is executed as a clearly separated phase.
+ROLE: implementation Worker. DESIGN GOAL: one owner in HTTPAdapter for "which timeout applies to this send",
+the default held by the adapter, validated on construction. BEHAVIOR: the exit criteria above.
+TESTING: test-first; characterize the current per-call timeout resolution before moving it.
+PRESERVE/NON-GOALS: as above; match the module's grain (plain attributes, `__attrs__` for pickling).
+RETURN: code + tests + design reasoning; met | partially_met | invalidated | blocked.
+
+## Open assumptions (unproven — carried, not filed)
+
+- urllib3's Timeout validates negative/non-numeric values on construction (falsified if a bad default
+  constructs) — relied on for fail-fast validation.
+
+## Open Guide TODO
+
+- [x] Supersede or honor the recorded decision → honor it; default lives on the adapter (product owner).
+- [x] Prove the default applies through every entry path (request, send, redirects) with Session untouched.
+- [x] File the adapter-level decision beside adapters.py (what it rules out: per-component merge, None-as-opt-out).
+
+## Last evaluated result
+
+met — measured by the Guide: full suite 645 passed, only the 4 known environmental TestTimeout connect
+failures (baseline 615 passed + 30 new). sessions.py diff empty. Default reaches urllib3 through
+Session.request, direct Session.send, and every redirect hop (test_adapters.py). Invalid default fails at
+construction; pickling keeps it; old pickles get None. Records: src/requests/adapters.py.md (new),
+src/requests/sessions.py.md (caveat superseded, decision reaffirmed), both anchored.
+Panel-plan declined: no subagent facility; Worker phase executed as a separate phase.
