@@ -1120,6 +1120,35 @@ coffee.
 
     r = requests.get('https://github.com', timeout=None)
 
+Default timeout for a Session
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+To give every request made through a :class:`Session <requests.Session>` a
+timeout without repeating it on each call, set it on the transport adapter the
+session sends through, and mount that adapter for both schemes::
+
+    from requests.adapters import HTTPAdapter
+
+    s = requests.Session()
+    adapter = HTTPAdapter(timeout=(3.05, 27))
+    s.mount('https://', adapter)
+    s.mount('http://', adapter)
+
+    s.get('https://github.com')              # uses (3.05, 27)
+    s.get('https://github.com', timeout=60)  # uses 60 for this call only
+
+The default applies to every request that adapter sends, including each
+redirect hop and requests sent with :meth:`Session.send
+<requests.Session.send>`. A call that passes its own ``timeout`` uses it as a
+whole; it is not merged with the default. Because ``timeout=None`` means "not
+given", it gets the default too: to let a single call wait forever, pass
+``timeout=(None, None)``. An invalid default raises ``ValueError`` when the
+adapter is created.
+
+The timeout is deliberately not a :class:`Session <requests.Session>`
+attribute: a session holds HTTP state (headers, cookies, auth), while
+connection behaviour, timeouts included, belongs to the transport adapters.
+
 .. note:: The connect timeout applies to each connection attempt to an IP address.
           If multiple addresses exist for a domain name, the underlying ``urllib3`` will
           try each address sequentially until one successfully connects.
